00:33:04.990 --> 00:33:09.609
And of course I remember your story that in his audition, he did a somersault.
当然我还记得你们说过的一个故事，他在试镜时表演了一个后空翻。

00:33:09.609 --> 00:33:10.609
Yes.
对。

00:33:10.609 --> 00:33:13.329
I mean, the physical comedy was part of it from the beginning.
我是说，形体喜剧从一开始就是其中的一部分。

00:33:13.329 --> 00:33:20.410
Literally from the audition, he was doing like shoulder rolls across like people's like casting directors, you know, offices.
literalmente从试镜开始，他就在选角导演们的办公室里滚地翻跟头。

00:33:20.410 --> 00:33:22.130
Do you remember him being super game to do this, Chris?
你还记得他当时对做这些超级有热情吗，克里斯？

00:33:22.130 --> 00:33:25.009
Do you remember like, was this like getting the candy store for him too, was he like?
你还记得吗？这对他来说就像是进了糖果店一样兴奋吗？

00:33:25.009 --> 00:33:26.690
He was really, he was really excited.
他真的很兴奋。

00:33:26.690 --> 00:33:33.769
And you could tell there's so many little, just him kicking the trash can when he's upset walking down the street.
你能看出有好多小细节，比如他心情不好时走在街上踢垃圾桶。

00:33:33.769 --> 00:33:35.809
And hurting his foot, hurting his foot.
还弄伤了脚，弄伤了脚。

00:33:35.809 --> 00:33:38.349
And that lasts for a few steps.
而且那种痛感持续了好几步。

00:33:38.349 --> 00:33:43.349
He was, he took it as the gift that we were helping.
他把这当作我们正在提供的恩赐。

00:33:44.609 --> 00:33:54.890
The crying, and when that sequence begins and that sort of semi Darth Vader music kind of kicks in and takes in that sequence, that you know you're really in for the ride at that point.
当哭泣开始，当那种半《星球大战》式的达斯·维达音乐响起并主导整个桥段时，你就知道接下来绝对会让你大呼过瘾。

00:33:54.890 --> 00:33:57.410
Like that's such a satisfying moment when that sequence begins.
当那个桥段开始时，那种感觉太让人满足了。

00:33:57.410 --> 00:33:59.490
It's like, this whole episode has been leading to this.
就好像整集都在为这一刻做铺垫。

00:33:59.490 --> 00:34:00.609
This is gonna work.
这招绝对行得通。

00:34:00.609 --> 00:34:06.769
And the idea to play that all in that kind of white limbo space is really avant-garde and weird.
而且把这一切都设定在那种白色虚空空间里的想法非常前卫且怪异。

00:34:06.769 --> 00:34:10.610
Do you remember how we quite got, it's because it was the Darth Vader thing, which was kind of an important thing.
你还记得我们是怎么想出这个的吗？因为当时有达斯·维达的梗，这其实挺重要的。

00:34:10.610 --> 00:34:12.730
It's almost like the return of the shirt montage.
这有点像是衬衫蒙太奇的回归。

00:34:12.730 --> 00:34:19.289
It's like things that you can't do when there's 200 people on, you know, high on candy in a live taping.
这就像是当有200个人在现场录制、情绪高涨时你根本无法做到的事情。

00:34:19.289 --> 00:34:30.269
Like that is where the cow and the mother became like this weird cinematic hybrid of, you know, a sitcom, a classic sitcom with like all these cinematic elements.
这就是《老爸老妈浪漫史》变成这种怪异的电影混合体的地方——它把情景喜剧、经典情景喜剧与所有这些电影元素融合在了一起。

00:34:30.269 --> 00:34:31.110
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

00:34:31.110 --> 00:34:35.869
And no idea where that white background came from, but it was awesome.
虽然不知道那个白色背景是从哪来的，但它真的很棒。

00:34:35.869 --> 00:34:41.710
And then John Swire, the composer, just doing that perfect sort of, boom, boom, boom, boom.
然后作曲家约翰·斯威尔（John Swire）创作了那种完美的音效：咚，咚，咚，咚。

00:34:41.710 --> 00:34:44.230
Just caring, you know exactly what you're watching.
只要稍加留意，你就完全知道自己在看什么。

00:34:44.230 --> 00:34:48.349
I also liked how the suit was all dark, like an all black suit, basically.
我也很喜欢这套衣服全都是暗色系的，基本上就像一身黑的西装。

00:34:48.349 --> 00:34:51.269
Never would have said that, but never would have chosen that, but it's great.
我以前绝对不会这么说，也绝对不会选这套，但它真的很棒。

00:34:51.269 --> 00:34:52.349
It's so Darth Vader.
太像达斯·维达了。

00:34:52.349 --> 00:34:54.349
It's the suit Darth Vader would wear.
这就是达斯·维达会穿的西装。

00:34:54.349 --> 00:34:57.349
Speaking of clothes, this is a silly throwaway.
说到衣服，这只是个无伤大雅的小细节。

00:34:57.349 --> 00:34:59.639
I really like Marshall sweater.
我真的很喜欢马歇尔的毛衣。

00:34:59.639 --> 00:35:00.480
With a dog though.
不过上面还有只狗。

00:35:00.480 --> 00:35:02.199
With a little orange dog.
带着一只橙色的小狗。

00:35:02.199 --> 00:35:04.119
I did have a moment where I said, what's happening?
我当时确实愣了一下，心想：这怎么回事？

00:35:04.119 --> 00:35:04.960
Was that dog?
那是狗吗？

00:35:04.960 --> 00:35:06.079
I forgot to swear to the dog.
我忘了对那只狗发誓了。

00:35:06.079 --> 00:35:07.079
I like it.
我很喜欢。

00:35:07.079 --> 00:35:08.079
I thought it was cool.
我觉得挺酷的。

00:35:08.079 --> 00:35:09.360
I thought it was better than in my house.
我觉得比我家里那件好看。

00:35:09.360 --> 00:35:10.599
Oh, really?
哦，真的吗？

00:35:10.599 --> 00:35:11.480
I'm pro.
我投赞成票。

00:35:11.480 --> 00:35:14.239
I'm team Marshall sweater.
我是马歇尔毛衣粉丝队的一员。

00:35:14.239 --> 00:35:16.079
Fantastic drunk, Josh.
你喝醉的样子太棒了，乔希。

00:35:16.079 --> 00:35:19.199
And I mean that in the most respectful way.
我是以最崇敬的心情说这话的。

00:35:19.199 --> 00:35:21.159
That is really hard to do.
这真的很难做到。

00:35:21.159 --> 00:35:24.440
With just going back to the re-return.
我们回到那个“再次回归”的话题。

00:35:24.440 --> 00:35:31.760
I forgot how big, that's a big deal that we revealed that too, that he re-returned that night of the pilot.
我差点忘了那有多重磅，我们竟然在试播集当晚就让他再次回归了，这也是个大秘密。

00:35:31.760 --> 00:35:33.679
And then we dive back into the pilot.
然后我们又回到了试播集。

00:35:33.679 --> 00:35:38.840
I was like, fuck, I forgot that we also do that in this episode, like it's sort of like, do you know what I was hooked on?
我当时想：靠，我忘了我们在这集里也有这一出，就好像……你知道我被什么吸引了吗？

00:35:38.840 --> 00:35:40.079
There's a lot behind here.
这背后有很多门道。

00:35:40.079 --> 00:35:45.360
I was like, they've been drinking a lot in this bar, including Ranjit, who then drives that.
我心想：他们在酒吧里喝得太多了，包括兰吉特，他后来还开车。

00:35:45.360 --> 00:35:52.159
I was like, wait a minute, this can't be safe, that is a great observation, maybe that's a good dream.
我当时就想：等一下，这太不安全了吧——这观察得太精辟了，或许那只是个美好的梦。

00:35:52.159 --> 00:35:54.480
Another Atonement session, I guess.
我想，又是一场赎罪大会。

00:35:54.480 --> 00:35:55.840
Don't drink and drive, kids.
孩子们，切勿酒后驾车。

00:35:55.840 --> 00:35:57.039
Don't drink and drive.
切勿酒后驾车。

00:35:57.039 --> 00:35:59.880
Don't film people without them knowing.
不要在别人不知情的情况下偷拍他们。

00:35:59.880 --> 00:36:02.159
There's a lot of things to not do on this show.
在这部剧里，有很多事情是不能做的。

00:36:02.159 --> 00:36:03.000
Do you know what?
你知道吗？

00:36:03.000 --> 00:36:07.760
I mean, there's so many little funny things, and I mean, the white is so funny, but I loved.
我是说，有很多有趣的小细节，而且我是说，那个白色真的很搞笑，但我超喜欢。

00:36:07.760 --> 00:36:09.840
We're not quitting just because Ted's so far ahead.
我们不能因为泰德领先太多就放弃。

00:36:09.840 --> 00:36:11.320
And he says, I was winning.
他说：我在赢。

00:36:11.320 --> 00:36:12.159
I was winning.
我在赢。

00:36:12.159 --> 00:36:17.880
Like, no one has any idea how to play this game, except Marshall, which is probably not even a real game, but that made me laugh.
就像是，除了马歇尔之外，根本没人知道这游戏怎么玩，这可能甚至都不是个真正的游戏，但那把我逗笑了。

00:36:17.880 --> 00:36:19.800
The idea that there's mayonnaise and the cookies.
饼干里竟然有蛋黄酱这个设定。

00:36:19.800 --> 00:36:22.360
I mean, we're playing off the seven layer salad a little bit there.
我的意思是，我们多少有点在致敬七层沙拉。

00:36:22.360 --> 00:36:23.179
We're kind of calling it.
我们有点在点题。

00:36:23.179 --> 00:36:27.280
She puts mayonnaise and everything and she misses mayonnaise with sweet dishes.
她什么都放蛋黄酱，而且她还把蛋黄酱和甜点混在一起。

00:36:27.280 --> 00:36:30.440
The slide in of Marshall's mom is fantastic.
马歇尔妈妈的闪亮登场太棒了。

00:36:30.440 --> 00:36:32.519
Just dying inside.
内心简直尴尬到死。

00:36:32.519 --> 00:36:33.360
Yeah.
对啊。

00:36:33.360 --> 00:36:34.840
That was so good.
那段太棒了。

00:36:34.840 --> 00:36:40.519
Well, I just thought also this episode is a little bit like, there's got to be a term for it.
嗯，我只是觉得这一集也有点像——一定有个词来形容它。

00:36:40.519 --> 00:36:45.239
I call it like filling in the lore, but it's like how I met everyone else.
我把它叫做“补充背景传说”，但它就像是“我是如何结识其他所有人的”。

00:36:45.239 --> 00:36:46.159
Remember that episode?
还记得那一集吗？

00:36:46.159 --> 00:36:47.000
Yeah.
对啊。

00:36:47.000 --> 00:36:56.440
Like just, you know, you guys created a show, Craig, that had such an ability to make so many different moves.
就像是，你知道的，克雷格，你们创作了一部拥有如此强大叙事空间的剧集。

00:36:56.440 --> 00:37:01.159
You could zip forward, you could zip back, you could forget a piece of information, go, oh, I forgot to tell you this part.
你可以快进，也可以倒回，你可以忘掉某条信息，然后说：“哦，我忘了告诉你这部分了。”

00:37:01.159 --> 00:37:06.400
Like, you really granted yourself like a real superpower narratively.
就像，你们在叙事上真的赋予了自己一种真正的超能力。

00:37:06.400 --> 00:37:08.960
This episode had more of them than I remembered.
这一集里这种桥段比我记忆中还要多。

00:37:08.960 --> 00:37:13.360
Like, Victoria's being omitted and just cutting the black screen.
比如，维多利亚被省略了，然后直接切到黑屏。

00:37:13.360 --> 00:37:14.840
You know, that was great.
你知道，那太棒了。

00:37:14.840 --> 00:37:15.679
Right, right.
对的，对的。

00:37:15.679 --> 00:37:23.679
And that was out of necessity, I really, because I saw, I found a story that she told, and deep in a, again, like, Oh wow.
那确实是出于无奈，真的，因为我看到，我找到了一个她讲的故事，藏在一个……又是那种……哦哇。

00:37:23.679 --> 00:37:25.760
In the cobwebs of my map, of my Mac.
在我Mac的地图的蛛丝马迹里。

00:37:25.760 --> 00:37:27.119
And it was okay.
结果还行。

00:37:27.119 --> 00:37:27.960
It was okay.
还算过得去。

00:37:27.960 --> 00:37:28.800
So this was much better then.
所以这样处理好得多。

00:37:28.800 --> 00:37:29.800
It's much better to not say it.
不讲出来反而更好。

00:37:29.800 --> 00:37:31.400
Much better to just not say it.
不说出来真的好得多。

00:37:31.400 --> 00:37:32.320
So it was born of a necessity.
所以这是出于无奈才诞生的。

00:37:32.320 --> 00:37:45.000
But yeah, I feel like this was something, I think that's super power, Josh, that you talk about is really cool, because I think in later episodes and seasons, the storytelling, there was a little bit more discovery.
不过，是的，我觉得这也是一种……乔希你说的那个超能力真的很酷，因为我觉得在后来的剧集和季数中，这种叙事方式带有了更多探索的性质。

00:37:45.000 --> 00:37:46.000
Oh, here's what we can do.
哦，原来我们还可以这样。

00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:47.440
And you look at trilogy time.
你看《三部曲之恋》。

00:37:47.440 --> 00:37:48.800
You look at Harry Met everyone else.
你看《老爸老妈的浪漫史》里是怎么认识其他人的。

00:37:48.800 --> 00:37:54.039
You look at all these other flashback and ways that flashbacks and flash forward were used.
你看所有这些其他的倒叙和闪回、闪现的使用方式。

00:37:54.039 --> 00:38:00.800
The one where Saggot or where Olderted completely gets every moment wrong and can't remember things.
也就是萨吉特（Saggot）或者说老版泰德完全把每个时刻都记错了、什么也记不住的那一集。

00:38:00.800 --> 00:38:07.519
And I feel like this was just us still in the shallow end almost, but having a lot of fun as we're discovering it.
我觉得这就像是我们还在浅水区嬉戏，但在不断探索的过程中收获了极大的乐趣。

00:38:07.519 --> 00:38:24.119
I mean, there's a funny, I'm always struck by how invested Lily and Marshall are, especially in the early seasons in Ted and his lore and being a part of his story and getting him partnered off so they can be on that front porch together, which they haven't even talked about, but it's clearly at play.
我是说，有一个趣点——莉莉和马歇尔对泰德以及他的传说投入了如此之多的精力，这总是让我感到震惊，尤其是在前几季中，他们渴望成为他故事的一部分，想早点帮他找到另一半，这样他们就能一起坐在前廊上了——尽管他们甚至还没谈过这个，但这显然已经在计划之中了。

00:38:24.119 --> 00:38:27.159
And Marshall's hurt over, I thought you were vomit-free.
还有马歇尔受到的伤害：“我以为你自90年代起就没吐过呢。”

00:38:27.159 --> 00:38:30.480
Like you're not, you weren't- Oh my God, the betrayal of three.
就好像你没有……你曾经……天啊，这是对三的背叛。

00:38:30.480 --> 00:38:38.480
It was a discussion in the room, as I recall, like, but wait, we can't tell the story because Ted has vomit-free since 90s.
我记得我们在编剧室里讨论过，就像是：但是等等，我们不能这么讲，因为泰德自90年代起就没吐过。

00:38:38.480 --> 00:38:43.039
Is that funny that that's your grown-up professional job sitting around with other grown-ups?
把这当作你成年后的专业工作，和其他成年人坐在一起讨论这些，是不是觉得挺荒唐的？

00:38:43.039 --> 00:38:47.039
Like, no, we established that he was vomit-free since 93.
就像：不，我们已经设定过他自93年起就没吐过。

00:38:47.039 --> 00:38:48.039
Sorry.
抱歉。

00:38:48.039 --> 00:38:49.039
We can't possibly...
我们绝对不能……

00:38:49.039 --> 00:38:51.360
How do we get around this?
我们怎么绕过这个坎？

00:38:51.360 --> 00:38:59.039
This is just for people who love the blooper reel, but I remember I could not say the green testicle story thing.
这只是给那些喜欢NG花絮的人准备的，但我记得我当时怎么也说不出“绿色睾丸”那个故事。

00:38:59.039 --> 00:39:02.719
Like on the blooper reel, there's like, I say it like five times in the wrong way.
就像在NG花絮里，我有大概五次都说错了。

00:39:02.719 --> 00:39:03.719
Like, I keep saying the wrong way.
我就一直说错。

00:39:03.719 --> 00:39:04.719
What got you about it?
是什么让你觉得好笑？

00:39:04.719 --> 00:39:05.719
When did you start laughing?
你是什么时候开始笑场 的？

00:39:05.719 --> 00:39:06.719
You just got wrong.
你就是说错了。

00:39:06.719 --> 00:39:07.719
I kept saying testicle in the wrong place.
我一直把“睾丸”这个词说错地方。

00:39:07.719 --> 00:39:08.719
Is it green testicle?
是叫绿色睾丸吗？

00:39:08.719 --> 00:39:09.719
Is that the thing?
是这个东西吗？

00:39:09.719 --> 00:39:10.719
Green testicle.
绿色睾丸。

00:39:10.719 --> 00:39:11.719
Green testicle, yeah.
绿色睾丸，对。

00:39:11.719 --> 00:39:12.719
I want to get that story.
我想把那个故事讲完。

00:39:12.719 --> 00:39:16.760
Someone who knows the blooper reel better than I do will have to look at season one bloopers.
对花絮比我更熟的人得去看看第一季的NG花絮了。

00:39:16.760 --> 00:39:17.760
Yeah.
对啊。

00:39:17.760 --> 00:39:24.320
That's from, I didn't tell, I didn't do the ultimate frisbee part, I think was, was either room or you Craig.
那是来自……我没有讲终极飞盘的部分，那个点子要么是编剧室想出来的，要么就是你，克雷格。

00:39:24.320 --> 00:39:44.639
Green testicles literally from a guy in my freshman dorm who had a, like a herniated test icle stuff like that and went into the, went into the, the health clinic and said, it's okay if we have to remove it, it's fine, you got another one and we can just replace, we You can just insert a green sphere into there, and then your life will be totally normal.
“绿色睾丸”字面意思来源于我大一宿舍里的一个家伙，他当时好像有疝气睾丸之类的毛病，然后去了健康诊所，说：“如果必须切除也没关系，没事的，反正你们还有另一个，我们可以直接替换——你们可以直接在里面植入一个绿色的球体，然后我的生活就完全正常了。”

00:39:44.639 --> 00:39:49.400
And he says he was so horrified and shocked that all I could think of to say was, do you have any other colors?
他说他当时吓坏了，也震惊极了，满脑子只想说：你们还有别的颜色吗？

00:39:49.400 --> 00:39:50.400
Yeah.
对啊。

00:39:50.400 --> 00:39:53.920
Oh my God, I forgot that completely.
天哪，我完全忘了这件事。

00:39:53.920 --> 00:39:55.880
That is the green testicle story.
这就是那个绿色睾丸的故事。

00:39:55.880 --> 00:39:57.719
I couldn't remember that.
我都想不起来了。

00:39:57.719 --> 00:39:59.039
Isn't it also so great?
你不觉得这也太棒了吗？

00:39:59.039 --> 00:40:03.519
Like obviously your comedic sensibility, your sense of structure, like all of that is a talent.
显然你的喜剧敏感度、结构感，所有这些都是一种天赋。

00:40:03.519 --> 00:40:07.400
That's part of why you're in a writer's room on a great show.
这也是为什么你能成为一部优秀剧集编剧室成员的部分原因。

00:40:07.400 --> 00:40:12.119
But also, every little weird thing that happened in your life might be admissible.
但同时，你生活中发生的每一件怪事都可能被采用。

00:40:12.119 --> 00:40:13.119
It can get on to TV.
它可以被搬上电视。

00:40:13.119 --> 00:40:14.119
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

00:40:14.119 --> 00:40:15.119
Yeah.
是啊。

00:40:15.119 --> 00:40:16.119
Do you know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

00:40:16.119 --> 00:40:17.119
Yeah.
对。

00:40:17.119 --> 00:40:18.880
Like, it's just like a collection of like, throw your best stories in the pot here.
就像，这就像是一个合集，把你们最好的故事都扔进这个大锅里。

